lder Content Restriction\";i:1065;s:15:\"Display Options\";i:1066;s:8:\"Redirect\";i:1067;s:19:\"Type of Restriction\";i:1068;s:16:\"Settings Default\";i:1069;s:11:\"Display For\";i:1070;s:15:\"Logged In Users\";i:1071;s:98:\"Checking only \"Logged In Users\" will show this %s to all logged in users, regardless of user role.\";i:1072;s:98:\"Checking any user role will show this %s only to users that have one of those user roles assigned.\";i:1073;s:24:\"Restriction Redirect URL\";i:1074;s:26:\"Enable Custom Redirect URL\";i:1075;s:59:\"Check if you wish to add a custom redirect URL for this %s.\";i:1076;s:19:\"Custom Redirect URL\";i:1077;s:108:\"Add a URL where you wish to redirect users that do not have access to this %s and try to access it directly.\";i:1078;s:20:\"Restriction Messages\";i:1079;s:22:\"Enable Custom Messages\";i:1080;s:53:\"Check if you wish to add custom messages for this %s.\";i:1081;s:29:\"Messages for logged-out users\";i:1082;s:28:\"Messages for logged-in users\";i:1083;s:19:\"Content Restriction\";i:1084;s:28:\"Content Restriction Settings\";i:1085;s:26:\"Enable Content Restriction\";i:1086;s:28:\"Activate Content Restriction\";i:1087;s:22:\"If you select \"Message\";i:1088;s:23:\"If you select \"Redirect\";i:1089;s:12:\"Redirect URL\";i:1090;s:28:\"Message for logged-out users\";i:1091;s:27:\"Message for logged-in users\";i:1092;s:24:\"Restricted Posts Preview\";i:1093;s:4:\"None\";i:1094;s:46:\"Show the first %s words of the post\\\'s content\";i:1095;s:38:\"Show the content before the \"more\" tag\";i:1096;s:98:\"Show a portion of the restricted post to logged-out users or users that are not allowed to see it.\";i:1097;s:15:\"No items found.\";i:1098;s:14:\"Show all dates\";i:1099;s:9:\"%1$s %2$d\";i:1100;s:9:\"List View\";i:1101;s:12:\"Excerpt View\";i:1102;s:10:\"%s pending\";i:1103;s:10:\"Select All\";i:1104;s:9:\"Unapprove\";i:1105;s:7:\"Approve\";i:1106;s:9:\"Firstname\";i:1107;s:8:\"Lastname\";i:1108;s:4:\"Role\";i:1109;s:11:\"User-status\";i:1110;s:47:\"Do you want to bulk approve the selected users?\";i:1111;s:49:\"Do you want to bulk unapprove the selected users?\";i:1112;s:46:\"Do you want to bulk delete the selected users?\";i:1113;s:8:\"Approved\";i:1114;s:10:\"Unapproved\";i:1115;s:14:\"Admin Approval\";i:1116;s:64:\"Your session has expired! Please refresh the page and try again.\";i:1117;s:27:\"User successfully approved!\";i:1118;s:29:\"User successfully unapproved!\";i:1119;s:26:\"User successfully deleted!\";i:1120;s:28:\"Users successfully approved!\";i:1121;s:39:\"Your account on %1$s has been approved!\";i:1122;s:8:\"approved\";i:1123;s:63:\"An administrator has just approved your account on %1$s (%2$s).\";i:1124;s:41:\"Your account on %1$s has been unapproved!\";i:1125;s:10:\"unapproved\";i:1126;s:65:\"An administrator has just unapproved your account on %1$s (%2$s).\";i:1127;s:99:\"<strong>ERROR</strong>: Your account has to be confirmed by an administrator before you can log in.\";i:1128;s:104:\"Your account has to be confirmed by an administrator before you can use the \"Password Recovery\" feature.\";i:1129;s:43:\"Your account has been successfully created!\";i:1130;s:95:\"The approval link is not valid! Please <a href=\"%s\"> log in </a> to approve the user manually. \";i:1131;s:16:\"Custom Redirects\";i:1132;s:19:\"User ID or Username\";i:1133;s:18:\"User ID / Username\";i:1134;s:56:\"Please select and enter the ID or username of your user.\";i:1135;s:13:\"Redirect Type\";i:1136;s:113:\"Can contain the following dynamic tags:{{homeurl}}, {{siteurl}}, {{user_id}}, {{user_nicename}}, {{http_referer}}\";i:1137;s:2:\"ID\";i:1138;s:25:\"Individual User Redirects\";i:1139;s:10:\"... Choose\";i:1140;s:19:\"Select a user role.\";i:1141;s:25:\"User Role based Redirects\";i:1142;s:16:\"Global Redirects\";i:1143;s:42:\"Redirect Default WordPress Forms and Pages\";i:1144;s:19:\"How does this work?\";i:1145;s:62:\"<pre>User ID / Username</pre><pre>Redirect</pre><pre>URL</pre>\";i:1146;s:53:\"<pre>User Role</pre><pre>Redirect</pre><pre>URL</pre>\";i:1147;s:33:\"<pre>Redirect</pre><pre>URL</pre>\";i:1148;s:96:\"These redirects happen after a successful action, like registration or after a successful login.\";i:1149;s:57:\"Which redirect happens depends on the following priority:\";i:1150;s:62:\"Multiple Registration and Edit Profile form settings Redirects\";i:1151;s:210:\"Individual redirects defined in shortcodes; <strong><em>redirect_priority=\\\"top\\\"</em></strong> parameter can be added in any shortcode, then that shortcode redirect will have priority over all other redirects.\";i:1152;s:42:\"Redirect Default WordPress forms and pages\";i:1153;s:100:\"With these you can redirect various WordPress forms and pages to pages created with profile builder.\";i:1154;s:31:\"Available tags for dynamic URLs\";i:1155;s:75:\"You use the following tags in your URLs to redirect users to various pages.\";i:1156;s:48:\"generates a url of the current website homepage.\";i:1157;s:146:\"in WordPress the <a target=\'_blank\' href=\'https://codex.wordpress.org/Function_Reference/site_url\'>site url</a> can be different then the home url\";i:1158;s:18:\"the ID of the user\";i:1159;s:140:\"the URL sanitized version of the username, the user nicename can be safely used in URLs since it can\'t contain special characters or spaces.\";i:1160;s:38:\"the URL of the previously visited page\";i:1161;s:34:\"You can\'t add duplicate redirects!\";i:1162;s:7:\"Modules\";i:1163;s:73:\"Here you can activate / deactivate available modules for Profile Builder.\";i:1164;s:16:\"Name/Description\";i:1165;s:6:\"Status\";i:1166;s:27:\"Multiple Registration Forms\";i:1167;s:27:\"Multiple Edit-profile Forms\";i:1168;s:12:\"User Listing\";i:1169;s:16:\"Email Customizer\";i:1170;s:15:\"Repeater Fields\";i:1171;s:22:\"Admin Email Customizer\";i:1172;s:31:\"Admin Email Customizer Settings\";i:1173;s:90:\"These settings are also replicated in the \"User Email Customizer\" settings-page upon save.\";i:1174;s:11:\"From (name)\";i:1175;s:21:\"From (reply-to email)\";i:1176;s:95:\"Must be a valid email address or the tag {{reply_to}} which defaults to the administrator email\";i:1177;s:15:\"Common Settings\";i:1178;s:101:\"<p>New subscriber on {{site_name}}.</p>\\n<p>Username:{{username}}</p>\\n<p>E-mail:{{user_email}}</p>\\n\";i:1179;s:13:\"Email Subject\";i:1180;s:12:\"Enable email\";i:1181;s:59:\"Default Registration & Registration with Email Confirmation\";i:1182;s:258:\"<p>New subscriber on {{site_name}}.</p>\\n<p>Username:{{username}}</p>\\n<p>E-mail:{{user_email}}</p>\\n<p>The Admin Approval feature was activated at the time of registration,\\nso please remember that you need to approve this user before he/she can log in!</p>\";i:1183;s:32:\"Registration with Admin Approval\";i:1184;s:131:\"<p>{{username}} has requested a password change via the password reset feature.</p>\\n<p>His/her new password is: {{password}}</p>\\n\";i:1185;s:42:\"Admin Notification for User Password Reset\";i:1186;s:21:\"User Email Customizer\";i:1187;s:30:\"User Email Customizer Settings\";i:1188;s:91:\"These settings are also replicated in the \"Admin Email Customizer\" settings-page upon save.\";i:1189;s:100:\"<h3>Welcome to {{site_name}}!</h3>\\n<p>Your username is:{{username}} and password:{{password}}</p>\\n\";i:1190;s:20:\"Default Registration\";i:1191;s:174:\"<p>To activate your user, please click the following link:<br/>\\n{{{activation_link}}}</p>\\n<p>After you activate, you will receive another email with your credentials.</p>\\n\";i:1192;s:37:\"[{{site_name}}] Activate {{username}}\";i:1193;s:36:\"Registration with Email Confirmation\";i:1194;s:214:\"<h3>Welcome to {{site_name}}!</h3>\\n<p>Your username is:{{username}} and password:{{password}}</p>\\n<p>Before you can access your account, an administrator needs to approve it. You will be notified via email.</p>\\n\";i:1195;s:55:\"A new account has been created for you on {{site_name}}\";i:1196;s:109:\"<h3>Good News!</h3>\\n<p>An administrator has just approved your account: {{username}} on {{site_name}}.</p>\\n\";i:1197;s:48:\"Your account on {{site_name}} has been approved!\";i:1198;s:26:\"User Approval Notification\";i:1199;s:122:\"<h3>Hello,</h3>\\n<p>Unfortunatelly an administrator has just unapproved your account: {{username}} on {{site_name}}.</p>\\n\";i:1200;s:50:\"Your account on {{site_name}} has been unapproved!\";i:1201;s:28:\"Unapproved User Notification\";i:1202;s:286:\"<p>Someone requested that the password be reset for the following account: {{site_name}}<br/>\\nUsername: {{username}}</p>\\n<p>If this was a mistake, just ignore this email and nothing will happen.</p>\\n<p>To reset your password, visit the following address:<br/>\\n{{{reset_link}}}</p>\\n\";i:1203;s:30:\"[{{site_name}}] Password Reset\";i:1204;s:20:\"Password Reset Email\";i:1205;s:51:\"<p>You have successfully reset your password.</p>\\n\";i:1206;s:43:\"[{{site_name}}] Password Reset Successfully\";i:1207;s:28:\"Password Reset Success Email\";i:1208;s:327:\"<h3>Hi {{username}},</h3>\\n<p>This notice confirms that your email was changed on {{site_name}}.</p>\\n<p>If you did not change your email, please contact the Site Administrator at %s</p>\\n<p>This email has been sent to {{user_email}}</p>\\n<p>Regards,<br>\\nAll at {{site_name}}<br>\\n<a href=\\\"{{site_url}}\\\">{{site_url}}</a></p>\";i:1209;s:38:\"[{{site_name}}] Notice of Email Change\";i:1210;s:34:\"Changed Email Address Notification\";i:1211;s:14:\"Available Tags\";i:1212;s:16:\"User Fields Tags\";i:1213;s:8:\"Site Url\";i:1214;s:9:\"Site Name\";i:1215;s:7:\"User Id\";i:1216;s:15:\"User Role Label\";i:1217;s:8:\"Reply To\";i:1218;s:8:\"Blog URL\";i:1219;s:14:\"Activation Key\";i:1220;s:14:\"Activation Url\";i:1221;s:15:\"Activation Link\";i:1222;s:9:\"Reset Key\";i:1223;s:9:\"Reset Url\";i:1224;s:10:\"Reset Link\";i:1225;s:16:\"Approve User Url\";i:1226;s:17:\"Approve User Link\";i:1227;s:60:\"You need to specify the title of the form before creating it\";i:1228;s:23:\"<pre>Title (Type)</pre>\";i:1229;s:16:\"Delete all items\";i:1230;s:10:\"Delete all\";i:1231;s:17:\"Registration Form\";i:1232;s:25:\"Add new Registration Form\";i:1233;s:27:\"Edit the Registration Forms\";i:1234;s:21:\"New Registration Form\";i:1235;s:18:\"Registration Forms\";i:1236;s:26:\"View the Registration Form\";i:1237;s:29:\"Search the Registration Forms\";i:1238;s:26:\"No Registration Form found\";i:1239;s:36:\"No Registration Forms found in trash\";i:1240;s:9:\"Shortcode\";i:1241;s:60:\"The shortcode will be available after you publish this form.\";i:1242;s:65:\"Use this shortcode on the page you want the form to be displayed:\";i:1243;s:89:\"<span style=\"color:red;\">Note:</span> changing the form title also changes the shortcode!\";i:1244;s:14:\"Form Shortcode\";i:1245;s:8:\"Set Role\";i:1246;s:131:\"Choose what role the user will have after (s)he registered<br/>If not specified, defaults to the role set in the WordPress settings\";i:1247;s:20:\"Automatically Log In\";i:1248;s:242:\"Whether to automatically log in the newly registered user or not<br/>Only works on single-sites without \"Admin Approval\" and \"Email Confirmation\" features activated<br/>WARNING: Caching the registration form will make automatic login not work\";i:1249;s:54:\"Whether to redirect the user to a specific page or not\";i:1250;s:16:\"Display Messages\";i:1251;s:57:\"Allowed time to display any success messages (in seconds)\";i:1252;s:3:\"URL\";i:1253;s:136:\"Specify the URL of the page users will be redirected once registered using this form<br/>Use the following format: http://www.mysite.com\";i:1254;s:21:\"After Registration...\";i:1255;s:25:\"Add New Field to the List\";i:1256;s:67:\"Choose one of the supported fields you manage <a href=\"%s\">here</a>\";i:1257;s:17:\"Edit-profile Form\";i:1258;s:25:\"Add new Edit-profile Form\";i:1259;s:27:\"Edit the Edit-profile Forms\";i:1260;s:21:\"New Edit-profile Form\";i:1261;s:18:\"Edit-profile Forms\";i:1262;s:26:\"View the Edit-profile Form\";i:1263;s:29:\"Search the Edit-profile Forms\";i:1264;s:26:\"No Edit-profile Form found\";i:1265;s:36:\"No Edit-profile Forms found in trash\";i:1266;s:152:\"Specify the URL of the page users will be redirected once they updated their profile using this form<br/>Use the following format: http://www.mysite.com\";i:1267;s:23:\"After Profile Update...\";i:1268;s:20:\"Add new User Listing\";i:1269;s:21:\"Edit the User Listing\";i:1270;s:16:\"New User Listing\";i:1271;s:21:\"View the User Listing\";i:1272;s:23:\"Search the User Listing\";i:1273;s:21:\"No User Listing found\";i:1274;s:30:\"No User Listing found in trash\";i:1275;s:0:\"\";i:1276;s:93:\"%s is also activated. You need to deactivate it before activating this version of the plugin.\";i:1277;s:7:\"Add-Ons\";i:1278;s:19:\"Recommended Plugins\";i:1279;s:4:\"Free\";i:1280;s:200:\"Translate your Profile Builder forms with a WordPress translation plugin that anyone can use. It offers a simpler way to translate WordPress sites, with full support for WooCommerce and site builders.\";i:1281;s:8:\"Activate\";i:1282;s:10:\"Deactivate\";i:1283;s:35:\"Plugin is <strong>inactive</strong>\";i:1284;s:33:\"Plugin is <strong>active</strong>\";i:1285;s:11:\"Install Now\";i:1286;s:48:\"Compatible with your version of Profile Builder.\";i:1287;s:89:\"Could not install plugin. Retry or <a href=\\\"%s\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">install manually</a>.\";i:1288;s:93:\"Accept user payments, create subscription plans and restrict content on your membership site.\";i:1289;s:29:\"Downloading and installing...\";i:1290;s:21:\"Installation complete\";i:1291;s:16:\"Add-On is Active\";i:1292;s:25:\"Add-On has been activated\";i:1293;s:13:\"Retry Install\";i:1294;s:33:\"Add-On is <strong>active</strong>\";i:1295;s:35:\"Add-On is <strong>inactive</strong>\";i:1296;s:28:\"Add-On has been deactivated.\";i:1297;s:81:\"Something went wrong, we could not connect to the server. Please try again later.\";i:1298;s:38:\"Available in Hobbyist and Pro Versions\";i:1299;s:25:\"Available in All Versions\";i:1300;s:10:\"Learn More\";i:1301;s:12:\"Download Now\";i:1302;s:23:\"Upgrade Profile Builder\";i:1303;s:35:\"Not compatible with Profile Builder\";i:1304;s:52:\"Not compatible with your version of Profile Builder.\";i:1305;s:41:\"Minimum required Profile Builder version:\";i:1306;s:89:\"Could not install add-on. Retry or <a href=\\\"%s\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">install manually</a>.\";i:1307;s:40:\"Show/Hide the Admin Bar on the Front-End\";i:1308;s:18:\"Admin Bar Settings\";i:1309;s:75:\"Choose which user roles view the admin bar in the front-end of the website.\";i:1310;s:9:\"User-Role\";i:1311;s:10:\"Visibility\";i:1312;s:4:\"Show\";i:1313;s:4:\"Hide\";i:1314;s:141:\"Login is set to be done using the E-mail. This field will NOT appear in the front-end! ( you can change these settings under the \\\"%s\\\" tab )\";i:1315;s:16:\"General Settings\";i:1316;s:65:\"Display name publicly as - only appears on the Edit Profile page!\";i:1317;s:53:\"Blog Details - only appears on the Registration page!\";i:1318;s:82:\"<strong>ERROR</strong>: The password must have the minimum length of %s characters\";i:1319;s:9:\"Very weak\";i:1320;s:71:\"<strong>ERROR</strong>: The password must have a minimum strength of %s\";i:1321;s:9:\"Add Field\";i:1322;s:13:\"Save Settings\";i:1323;s:196:\"If you enjoy using <strong> %1$s </strong> please <a href=\\\"%2$s\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">rate us on WordPress.org</a>. More happy users means more features, less bugs and better support for everyone. \";i:1324;s:34:\"View Profile Builder documentation\";i:1325;s:4:\"Docs\";i:1326;s:116:\"Check out the Customization Toolbox add-on which packs the most popular customization requests from Profile Builder.\";i:1327;s:11:\"See details\";i:1328;s:20:\"Dismiss this notice.\";i:1329;s:17:\"Basic Information\";i:1330;s:36:\"<strong>Profile Builder </strong> %s\";i:1331;s:73:\"The best way to add front-end registration, edit profile and login forms.\";i:1332;s:68:\"Speed up the setup process by automatically creating the form pages:\";i:1333;s:17:\"Create Form Pages\";i:1334;s:68:\"You can see all the pages with Profile Builder form shortcodes here:\";i:1335;s:15:\"View Form Pages\";i:1336;s:10:\"Login Form\";i:1337;s:51:\"Friction-less login using %s shortcode or a widget.\";i:1338;s:71:\"Beautiful registration forms fully customizable using the %s shortcode.\";i:1339;s:17:\"Edit Profile Form\";i:1340;s:55:\"Straight forward edit profile forms using %s shortcode.\";i:1341;s:14:\"Extra Features\";i:1342;s:114:\"Features that give you more control over your users, increased security and help you fight user registration spam.\";i:1343;s:21:\"Enable extra features\";i:1344;s:16:\"Recover Password\";i:1345;s:68:\"Allow users to recover their password in the front-end using the %s.\";i:1346;s:18:\"Admin Approval (*)\";i:1347;s:121:\"You decide who is a user on your website. Get notified via email or approve multiple users at once from the WordPress UI.\";i:1348;s:18:\"Email Confirmation\";i:1349;s:126:\"Make sure users sign up with genuine emails. On registration users will receive a notification to confirm their email address.\";i:1350;s:111:\"Restrict users from accessing certain pages, posts or custom post types based on user role or logged-in status.\";i:1351;s:42:\"Minimum Password Length and Strength Meter\";i:1352;s:115:\"Eliminate weak passwords altogether by setting a minimum password length and enforcing a certain password strength.\";i:1353;s:28:\"Login with Email or Username\";i:1354;s:76:\"Allow users to log in with their email or username when accessing your site.\";i:1355;s:12:\"Roles Editor\";i:1356;s:72:\"Add, remove, clone and edit roles and also capabilities for these roles.\";i:1357;s:41:\"Customize Your Forms The Way You Want (*)\";i:1358;s:88:\"With Extra Profile Fields you can create the exact registration form your project needs.\";i:1359;s:62:\"Extra Profile Fields are available in Hobbyist or PRO versions\";i:1360;s:29:\"Get started with extra fields\";i:1361;s:13:\"Avatar Upload\";i:1362;s:15:\"Generic Uploads\";i:1363;s:23:\"Agree To Terms Checkbox\";i:1364;s:10:\"Datepicker\";i:1365;s:10:\"Timepicker\";i:1366;s:11:\"Colorpicker\";i:1367;s:9:\"reCAPTCHA\";i:1368;s:14:\"Country Select\";i:1369;s:15:\"Currency Select\";i:1370;s:15:\"Timezone Select\";i:1371;s:20:\"Input / Hidden Input\";i:1372;s:6:\"Select\";i:1373;s:8:\"Textarea\";i:1374;s:10:\"Validation\";i:1375;s:3:\"Map\";i:1376;s:4:\"HTML\";i:1377;s:21:\"Powerful Modules (**)\";i:1378;s:98:\"Everything you will need to manage your users is probably already available using the Pro Modules.\";i:1379;s:19:\"Enable your modules\";i:1380;s:31:\"Find out more about PRO Modules\";i:1381;s:159:\"Easy to edit templates for listing your website users as well as creating single user pages. Shortcode based, offering many options to customize your listings.\";i:1382;s:137:\"To create a page containing the users registered to this current site/blog, insert the following shortcode in a page of your chosing: %s.\";i:1383;s:119:\"Personalize all emails sent to your users or admins. On registration, email confirmation, admin approval / un-approval.\";i:1384;s:146:\"Keep your users out of the WordPress dashboard, redirect them to the front-page after login or registration, everything is just a few clicks away.\";i:1385;s:141:\"Set up multiple registration forms with different fields for certain user roles. Capture different information from different types of users.\";i:1386;s:143:\"Allow different user roles to edit their specific information. Set up multiple edit-profile forms with different fields for certain user roles.\";i:1387;s:126:\"Set up a repeating group of fields on register and edit profile forms. Limit the number of repeated groups for each user role.\";i:1388;s:59:\" * only available in the %1$sHobbyist and Pro versions%2$s.\";i:1389;s:45:\"** only available in the %1$sPro version%2$s.\";i:1390;s:14:\"Quick Feedback\";i:1391;s:102:\"Because we care about our clients, please leave us feedback on why you are no longer using our plugin.\";i:1392;s:24:\"Lacking certain features\";i:1393;s:35:\"What feature would you like to see?\";i:1394;s:11:\"Hard to use\";i:1395;s:40:\"How can we improve our user experience ?\";i:1396;s:22:\"Unsatisfactory support\";i:1397;s:19:\"Please tell us more\";i:1398;s:18:\"Poor Documentation\";i:1399;s:30:\"Tell us what you couldn\'t find\";i:1400;s:19:\"Submit & Deactivate\";i:1401;s:19:\"Skip and Deactivate\";i:1402;s:21:\"Submit and Deactivate\";i:1403;s:9:\"Admin Bar\";i:1404;s:15:\"Private Website\";i:1405;s:11:\"User Emails\";i:1406;s:20:\"Administrator Emails\";i:1407;s:24:\"Profile Builder Settings\";i:1408;s:53:\"Load Profile Builder\'s own CSS file in the front-end:\";i:1409;s:40:\"You can find the default file here: %1$s\";i:1410;s:33:\"\\\"Email Confirmation\\\" Activated:\";i:1411;s:145:\"This works with front-end forms only. Recommended to redirect WP default registration to a Profile Builder one using \\\"Custom Redirects\\\" module.\";i:1412;s:98:\"You can find a list of unconfirmed email addresses %1$sUsers > All Users > Email Confirmation%2$s.\";i:1413;s:36:\"\\\"Email Confirmation\\\" Landing Page:\";i:1414;s:14:\"Existing Pages\";i:1415;s:240:\"Specify the page where the users will be directed when confirming the email account. This page can differ from the register page(s) and can be changed at any time. If none selected, a simple confirmation page will be displayed for the user.\";i:1416;s:29:\"\\\"Admin Approval\\\" Activated:\";i:1417;s:75:\"You can find a list of users at %1$sUsers > All Users > Admin Approval%2$s.\";i:1418;s:32:\"\\\"Admin Approval\\\" on User Role:\";i:1419;s:53:\"Select on what user roles to activate Admin Approval.\";i:1420;s:27:\"\\\"Roles Editor\\\" Activated:\";i:1421;s:62:\"You can add / edit user roles at %1$sUsers > Roles Editor%2$s.\";i:1422;s:27:\"\\\"Admin Approval\\\" Feature:\";i:1423;s:193:\"You decide who is a user on your website. Get notified via email or approve multiple users at once from the WordPress UI. Enable Admin Approval by upgrading to %1$sHobbyist or PRO versions%2$s.\";i:1424;s:27:\"Allow Users to Log in With:\";i:1425;s:18:\"Username and Email\";i:1426;s:71:\"\\\"Username and Email\\\" - users can Log In with both Username and Email.\";i:1427;s:51:\"\\\"Username\\\" - users can Log In only with Username.\";i:1428;s:45:\"\\\"Email\\\" - users can Log In only with Email.\";i:1429;s:24:\"Minimum Password Length:\";i:1430;s:87:\"Enter the minimum characters the password should have. Leave empty for no minimum limit\";i:1431;s:26:\"Minimum Password Strength:\";i:1432;s:8:\"Disabled\";i:1433;s:11:\"Form Fields\";i:1434;s:18:\"Manage Form Fields\";i:1435;s:39:\"Choose one of the supported field types\";i:1436;s:81:\". Extra Field Types are available in <a href=\\\"%s\\\">Hobbyist or PRO versions</a>.\";i:1437;s:245:\"Use this in conjunction with WordPress functions to display the value in the page of your choosing<br/>Auto-completed but in some cases editable (in which case it must be unique)<br/>Changing this might take long in case of a very big user-count\";i:1438;s:232:\"Use this in conjunction with WordPress functions to display the value in the page of your choosing<br/>Auto-completed but in some cases editable (in which case it must be unique)<br/>Changing this will only affect subsequent entries\";i:1439;s:11:\"Field Title\";i:1440;s:18:\"Title of the field\";i:1441;s:9:\"Meta-name\";i:1442;s:154:\"A unique, auto-generated ID for this particular field<br/>You can use this in conjuction with filters to target this element if needed<br/>Can\'t be edited\";i:1443;s:79:\"Enter a (detailed) description of the option for end users to read<br/>Optional\";i:1444;s:9:\"Row Count\";i:1445;s:85:\"Specify the number of rows for a \'Textarea\' field<br/>If not specified, defaults to 5\";i:1446;s:24:\"Allowed Image Extensions\";i:1447;s:144:\"Specify the extension(s) you want to limit to upload<br/>Example: .ext1,.ext2,.ext3<br/>If not specified, defaults to: .jpg,.jpeg,.gif,.png (.*)\";i:1448;s:25:\"Allowed Upload Extensions\";i:1449;s:160:\"Specify the extension(s) you want to limit to upload<br/>Example: .ext1,.ext2,.ext3<br/>If not specified, defaults to all WordPress allowed file extensions (.*)\";i:1450;s:11:\"Avatar Size\";i:1451;s:101:\"Enter a value (between 20 and 200) for the size of the \'Avatar\'<br/>If not specified, defaults to 100\";i:1452;s:11:\"Date-format\";i:1453;s:241:\"Specify the format of the date when using Datepicker<br/>Valid options: mm/dd/yy, mm/yy/dd, dd/yy/mm, dd/mm/yy, yy/dd/mm, yy/mm/dd, mm-dd-yy, yy-mm-dd, D, dd M yy, D, d M y, DD, dd-M-y, D, d M yy, @<br/>If not specified, defaults to mm/dd/yy\";i:1454;s:18:\"Terms of Agreement\";i:1455;s:184:\"Enter a detailed description of the temrs of agreement for the user to read.<br/>Links can be inserted by using standard HTML syntax: &lt;a href=\\\"custom_url\\\"&gt;custom_text&lt;/a&gt;\";i:1456;s:152:\"Enter a comma separated list of values<br/>This can be anything, as it is hidden from the user, but should not contain special characters or apostrophes\";i:1457;s:6:\"Labels\";i:1458;s:63:\"Enter a comma separated list of labels<br/>Visible for the user\";i:1459;s:14:\"reCAPTCHA Type\";i:1460;s:146:\"Choose the <a href=\\\"https://developers.google.com/recaptcha/docs/versions\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">type of reCAPTCHA</a> you wish to add to this site.\";i:1461;s:8:\"Site Key\";i:1462;s:116:\"The site key from Google, <a href=\\\"http://www.google.com/recaptcha\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">www.google.com/recaptcha</a>\";i:1463;s:10:\"Secret Key\";i:1464;s:118:\"The secret key from Google, <a href=\\\"http://www.google.com/recaptcha\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">www.google.com/recaptcha</a>\";i:1465;s:19:\"Display on PB forms\";i:1466;s:8:\"PB Login\";i:1467;s:11:\"PB Register\";i:1468;s:19:\"PB Recover Password\";i:1469;s:58:\"Select on which Profile Builder forms to display reCAPTCHA\";i:1470;s:27:\"Display on default WP forms\";i:1471;s:16:\"Default WP Login\";i:1472;s:19:\"Default WP Register\";i:1473;s:27:\"Default WP Recover Password\";i:1474;s:53:\"Select on which default WP forms to display reCAPTCHA\";i:1475;s:10:\"User Roles\";i:1476;s:73:\"Select which user roles to show to the user ( drag and drop to re-order )\";i:1477;s:16:\"User Roles Order\";i:1478;s:55:\"Save the user role order from the user roles checkboxes\";i:1479;s:26:\"Default value of the field\";i:1480;s:14:\"Default Option\";i:1481;s:54:\"Specify the option which should be selected by default\";i:1482;s:17:\"Default Option(s)\";i:1483;s:109:\"Specify the option which should be checked by default<br/>If there are multiple values, separate them with a \";i:1484;s:27:\"Default option of the field\";i:1485;s:20:\"Show Currency Symbol\";i:1486;s:93:\"Whether the currency symbol should be displayed after the currency name in the select option.\";i:1487;s:14:\"Show Post Type\";i:1488;s:58:\"Posts from what post type will be displayed in the select.\";i:1489;s:16:\"Allowable Values\";i:1490;s:169:\"Enter a comma separated list of possible values. Upon registration if the value provided by the user does not match one of these values, the user will not be registered.\";i:1491;s:13:\"Error Message\";i:1492;s:62:\"Set a custom error message that will be displayed to the user.\";i:1493;s:11:\"Time Format\";i:1494;s:24:\"Specify the time format.\";i:1495;s:19:\"Google Maps API Key\";i:1496;s:262:\"Enter your Google Maps API key ( <a href=\\\"https://console.developers.google.com/flows/enableapi?apiid=maps_backend\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">Get your API key</a> ). If more than one map fields are added to a form the API key from the first map displayed will be used.\";i:1497;s:16:\"Default Latitude\";i:1498;s:76:\"The latitude at which the map should be displayed when no pins are attached.\";i:1499;s:17:\"Default Longitude\";i:1500;s:77:\"The longitude at which the map should be displayed when no pins are attached.\";i:1501;s:18:\"Default Zoom Level\";i:1502;s:69:\"Add a number from 0 to 19. The higher the number the higher the zoom.\";i:1503;s:10:\"Map Height\";i:1504;s:22:\"The height of the map.\";i:1505;s:15:\"Default Content\";i:1506;s:29:\"Default value of the textarea\";i:1507;s:12:\"HTML Content\";i:1508;s:31:\"Add your HTML (or text) content\";i:1509;s:12:\"Phone Format\";i:1510;s:78:\"You can use: # for numbers, parentheses ( ), - sign, + sign, dot . and spaces.\";i:1511;s:18:\"Eg. (###) ###-####\";i:1512;s:49:\"Empty field won\'t check for correct phone number.\";i:1513;s:11:\"Heading Tag\";i:1514;s:44:\"Change heading field size on front-end forms\";i:1515;s:16:\"Min Number Value\";i:1516;s:59:\"Min allowed number value (0 to allow only positive numbers)\";i:1517;s:31:\"Leave it empty for no min value\";i:1518;s:16:\"Max Number Value\";i:1519;s:59:\"Max allowed number value (0 to allow only negative numbers)\";i:1520;s:31:\"Leave it empty for no max value\";i:1521;s:17:\"Number Step Value\";i:1522;s:85:\"Step value 1 to allow only integers, 0.1 to allow integers and numbers with 1 decimal\";i:1523;s:70:\"To allow multiple decimals use for eg. 0.01 (for 2 deciamls) and so on\";i:1524;s:123:\"You can also use step value to specify the legal number intervals (eg. step value 2 will allow only -4, -2, 0, 2 and so on)\";i:1525;s:33:\"Leave it empty for no restriction\";i:1526;s:8:\"Required\";i:1527;s:36:\"Whether the field is required or not\";i:1528;s:18:\"Overwrite Existing\";i:1529;s:156:\"Selecting \'Yes\' will add the field to the list, but will overwrite any other field in the database that has the same meta-name<br/>Use this at your own risk\";i:1530;s:21:\"Form Field Properties\";i:1531;s:33:\"Registration & Edit Profile Forms\";i:1532;s:28:\"Usernames cannot be changed.\";i:1533;s:10:\"First Name\";i:1534;s:9:\"Last Name\";i:1535;s:8:\"Nickname\";i:1536;s:24:\"Display name publicly as\";i:1537;s:12:\"Contact Info\";i:1538;s:3:\"AIM\";i:1539;s:8:\"Yahoo IM\";i:1540;s:20:\"Jabber / Google Talk\";i:1541;s:14:\"About Yourself\";i:1542;s:17:\"Biographical Info\";i:1543;s:93:\"Share a little biographical information to fill out your profile. This may be shown publicly.\";i:1544;s:19:\"Type your password.\";i:1545;s:26:\"Type your password again. \";i:1546;s:12:\"Blog Details\";i:1547;s:16:\"Select a Country\";i:1548;s:7:\"Bolivia\";i:1549;s:33:\"Bonaire, Saint Eustatius and Saba\";i:1550;s:22:\"British Virgin Islands\";i:1551;s:6:\"Brunei\";i:1552;s:10:\"Cape Verde\";i:1553;s:13:\"Cocos Islands\";i:1554;s:32:\"Democratic Republic of the Congo\";i:1555;s:10:\"East Timor\";i:1556;s:16:\"Falkland Islands\";i:1557;s:4:\"Iran\";i:1558;s:11:\"Ivory Coast\";i:1559;s:6:\"Kosovo\";i:1560;s:4:\"Laos\";i:1561;s:9:\"Macedonia\";i:1562;s:10:\"Micronesia\";i:1563;s:7:\"Moldova\";i:1564;s:11:\"North Korea\";i:1565;s:21:\"Palestinian Territory\";i:1566;s:21:\"Republic of the Congo\";i:1567;s:6:\"Russia\";i:1568;s:12:\"Saint Helena\";i:1569;s:12:\"Saint Martin\";i:1570;s:12:\"Sint Maarten\";i:1571;s:11:\"South Korea\";i:1572;s:5:\"Syria\";i:1573;s:6:\"Taiwan\";i:1574;s:8:\"Tanzania\";i:1575;s:19:\"U.S. Virgin Islands\";i:1576;s:7:\"Vatican\";i:1577;s:9:\"Venezuela\";i:1578;s:7:\"Vietnam\";i:1579;s:11:\"Albania Lek\";i:1580;s:19:\"Afghanistan Afghani\";i:1581;s:14:\"Argentina Peso\";i:1582;s:16:\"Australia Dollar\";i:1583;s:20:\"Azerbaijan New Manat\";i:1584;s:14:\"Bahamas Dollar\";i:1585;s:15:\"Barbados Dollar\";i:1586;s:16:\"Bangladeshi taka\";i:1587;s:13:\"Belarus Ruble\";i:1588;s:13:\"Belize Dollar\";i:1589;s:14:\"Bermuda Dollar\";i:1590;s:17:\"Bolivia Boliviano\";i:1591;s:40:\"Bosnia and Herzegovina Convertible Marka\";i:1592;s:13:\"Botswana Pula\";i:1593;s:12:\"Bulgaria Lev\";i:1594;s:11:\"Brazil Real\";i:1595;s:24:\"Brunei Darussalam Dollar\";i:1596;s:13:\"Cambodia Riel\";i:1597;s:13:\"Canada Dollar\";i: